  "taker_source_rule": "At decision time T, first require create_time<=T and logical_available_at<=T. A finalized REST taker row is real-time eligible only when the live/paper collector physically received it by T (received_at<=T). When both an eligible REST row and an archive row exist, use REST buy_sell_ratio; never replace it later with the archive value. When no eligible REST row exists, historical training, validation, final-test replay, and backfill use archive sum_taker_long_short_vol_ratio. Never average or blend sources, and never silently fill a missing selected-source value from the other source. Preserve source, received_at, logical_available_at, age, and missing masks. Taker parity blocking checks: complete expected-period coverage, normalized timestamp and alignment, missing-mask agreement, and REST buySellRatio = Q4(buyVol/sellVol) with Decimal ROUND_HALF_UP. Archive-versus-REST Q3 mismatch counts and raw absolute/relative residuals are mandatory report-only diagnostics and do not affect parity pass. This supersedes only A1's taker archive-versus-REST Q3 blocking requirement; global LS, top LS, OI, OI value and prediction parity requirements are unchanged. Stage-B training, validation and final testing use archive taker; later live-paper rows use causally received REST taker. This is an intentional documented source shift, not exact train/serve parity; accepted for research and paper replay only, with no predictive-equivalence claim. After Stage-B selection (no reselection), compare feature -> prediction -> entry on the 7 overlapping days with archive vs REST taker and record the result.",
